{
  "_about": "The wild animals and birds round the farm (scripts/wildlife.gd). tiers: the five rarities, commonest first; a fibre's tier sets the least a sweater knitted from it can be (knit_floor, 1 Common .. 5 Legendary on the knitting game's scale). animals: name, the tier, the fibre a comb gives (an item id in fibres; wild sheep give plain wool), the model and its loops' strides (metres a second at speed 1, printed by art/world_assets/wildlife/tripo_build.py), walk and run speeds, how many live in the world, the habitats they wander (names in habitats, [x, z, width, depth] in metres), how close she can come at a run or with the dog before they bolt (shy), the size of the box a click finds them by (click, metres), and the days their fur takes to grow back after a comb. shorn_model and shorn_stride: the naked model it shows from a comb until its fur is back, and its loops' strides (Alex, 2026-11-16). Commoner animals live nearer the farm and there are more of them; the rarer, the fewer and the further out (Alex, 2026-11-14: sheep the most common). birds: small flocks that peck about in their zone and fly off when she or the dog comes within flush metres. Every name is a draft until Alex approves it.",
